rts of the law  at least that's what I hope will happen  hopefully I'll still be able to make  prepare to cry for Dark Souls 2 Dark  Souls 2 is going to look amazing  graphically considering the new console  generation should roll in at the end of  next year it's hard to say whether the  game will be released as a next-gen  title regardless it will be released on  PC and reach its full graphical  potential on that platform a petition  was made for a release on Wii U but I  doubt it will be heard by Namco Bandai  let's finish with a talk about the  gameplay bear in mind that every souls  trailer hints of what we're going to see  in terms of gameplay Dark Souls 2 of  masks and Dragons shows strong  characterization and depicts a journey  the main character is dual wielding  which I expect we'll see in game  especially since Shibuya talks of  enhancing the action there will also be  a system in the game where the player  can keep a track of the clues they have  uncovered sounds a bit like a journal or  a quest log which I hope that they can  implement properly the new directors  have expressed interest in the notion of  snow and weather which almost make it  sound like the game could have our  dynamic weather system imagine how the  mood of the game could be enhanced if  you were travelling through a forest and  it started raining or snowing speaking  of the mood Shibuya expresses excitement  about the ocean or the sea as a Khan  that hasn't been done before in Seoul's  games in Japan it's an iconic idea that  when you're standing by the sea alone  you're often depressed this fits the  souls games pretty well the world design  team at from software is huge and a  focusing of making unique environments  this time around it seems like we'll be  able to travel through these  environments at speed as the team wants  to implement vehicles the only two that  have been suggested so far are ships and  chariots which should suit the fantasy  theme in terms of new enemies we have a  grotesquely obese enemy wielding sickles  a dwarf with the monstrous acts a giant  spider parasite that takes over human  bodies a black rider who punishes the  player for evil deeds and a relatively  normal enemy that it was apparently  top-secret this blind bandaged zombie  with a gaping open ribcage was not open  for discussion with the new director  finally we will see a return to server  based PvP in Dark Souls 2 like we had in  Demon Souls this will mean a better  online experience that just about sums  up everything that we know so far and  hopefully it hopes you get hyped in  other YouTube videos comments  communities and articles I've noticed a  lot of pessimism about Dark Souls 2  which I understand however it's not a  bad thing if the game takes risks we see  so many other franchises being rehashed  and repackaged as the same game every  year and I don't want the souls series  to die like that the game is going to  change but I want to see the series  evolve and I want to see the developers  learn something new every time they make  a new game that's how you keep a series  fresh and alive and I'm sure the game  will be more than just accessible anyway  thanks for watching guys I hope you  enjoyed the video
 

